"id":358084,"title":"","content":"Almost anything, but a favorite is...<br /> <br /> Dead Can Dance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T01:29:04-08:00","id":358126,"title":"","content":"Midnight Syndicate's a pretty good choice for background music. If you've ever been to a haunted house, the odds are good you've heard their work before. They theme each album after a different traditional haunted location, creating tone poems about the spooky old house on the hill or the abandoned insane asylum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T20:41:11-08:00","id":362045,"title":"","content":"Lustmord is good, dark stuff for Doomslaying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4680,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4680-bells","user":"Bells","date":".  spelling 03-30-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4680-bells","name":"Bells","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T23:14:52-08:00","id":362157,"title":"","content":"Working music tonight:<br /> <br /> Best of Millennium - Mark Snow<br /> The Final Breath Before November - Edison's Children<br /> March of Ghosts - Gazpacho<br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T06:29:59-08:00","id":362372,"title":"","content":"<br /> I like to use the soundtracks of &quot;The Crow&quot;, &quot;The Crow: City of Angels&quot;, and The Cure, Siouxie and the Banshees, for obvious reasons... Recently, I have enjoyed particularly two of Arcade Fire songs : &quot;Reflektor&quot; and &quot;Afterlife&quot;. This last song is especially significant for Wraith . The video also fits perfectly with the theme of the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4649-lauro1980","name":"lauro1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T22:17:05-08:00","id":363211,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path apparently made mood music playlists on youtube- the Wraith one actually features a lot of the artists suggested here, like Loreena McKennit and stuff from the Crow and Silent Hill: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLiNRTdSDh6-VHTCpGoMxn8C6y0Pzgb7A5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/playlist?lis...xn8C6y0Pzgb7A5</a><br /> <br /> Spooky!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T11:05:37-08:00","id":363685,"title":"","content":"Some Adam Hurst songs are fantastic for a Wraith game. It's easy to get into a decaying and melancholic setting with his music: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAwKGi7PIzQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAwKGi7PIzQ</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=idlfGrRToCE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=idlfGrRToCE</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:38:54-07:00","id":462234,"title":"","content":"Currently using a combination of Lustmord, Lamb of God &amp; Schindler's List","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4680-bells","name":"Bells","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:10:34-07:00","id":462261,"title":"","content":"Elend for the slowly unnerving parts (some of their more dissonant songs are perfect Harrowing material)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5c8XLBwynwA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5c8XLBwynwA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5c8XLBwynwA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5c8XLBwynwA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5c8XLBwynwA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bohren and Der Club Of Gore for the slow, relaxing parts (move through the city, taking a boatride on a Byway):<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zl5vpy__dQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zl5vpy__dQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zl5vpy__dQ </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zl5vpy__dQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zl5vpy__dQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Diamanda Galas for Harrowings:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEKuX8arORc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEKuX8arORc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEKuX8arORc </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEKuX8arORc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LEKuX8arORc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Come to think of it Galas would make a great soundtrack for a more Hell-themed Far Shore. And my Troupe foolishly wished to see the Fishers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:22:36-07:00","id":462347,"title":"","content":"quoting Real Dead Guy:<br /> <br /> You know the rooms underneath Stygia filled with dozens and dozens of bottle Spectres that they're trying to convert back to wraith-hood?<br /> <br /> They play Phil Collins in those rooms.<br /> <br /> Nothing but Phil Collins.<br /> <br /> Late-period solo Phil Collins.<br /> <br /> Forever.<br /> <br /> oh and, RDG if you read this &quot;Sussudio.&quot; , love ya buddy :P<br /> <br /> <br /> ok getting more serious hurmm...Tool, A Perfect Circle, The Silent Hill Score (mainly one to three), the Schindlers list score, The Wall by Pink Floyd... Oh And In Between Days/Make me Bad (the acoustic version of The Cure with Korn) its awesome to tell the story of a wraith and his shadow. i also use some korn....some Linkin Park (had an emo wraith..was fun because we all made fun of him xD), the 300 soundtrack, Marylin Manson, Nine Inch Nail's Ghosts, Dark City Soundtrack<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:24:42-07:00","id":462349,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Classical, music that's as old as some of the Relics in the place.</span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Night on Bald Mountain<br /> Funeral March of a Marionette<br /> Der Vampyre<br /> Danse Macabre<br /> Dreams of a Witches' Sabbath<br /> Totentaz<br /> Isle of the Dead<br /> Toccata and Fugue in D Minor<br /> March to the Scaffold</b></i><br /> Anyone's <i><b>Requiem</b></i>, but I love Mozart's the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 03-30-2015, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:40:58-07:00","id":462682,"title":"","content":"Just posted this on the Wraith the Oblivion group on Google+.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0FJNZyhRfA4\" data-code=\"0FJNZyhRfA4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0FJNZyhRfA4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T04:47:41-07:00","id":465920,"title":"","content":"The soundtrack to Alien 3 is the most beautifully haunting thing I've heard in a long time. I always loved that film, despite its flaws, and think the soundtrack was a big part of it.<br /> <br /> I recently spent time rediscovering the soundtrack while producing a track for a drag number, of all things! I was doing Sigourney Weaver in Alien 3, so used a combination of sound effects from the four films, plus an underscore of the opening music from Alien 3 specifically, before the whole thing became Christina Aguilera's 'Fighter' (I was appealing to a populist crowd...). The results are on YouTube, as it happens, but I digress.<br /> <br /> The blend of Catholicism, mediaevalism and occasional violence are great. Especially if there's a storm or spectral attack looming. It's also very cinematic, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T22:04:54-07:00","id":467002,"title":"","content":"Any of the more moody/sad pieces by Kajiura Yuki, mistress of Operatic Anime Music, will fit nicely.<br /> <br /> Point in fact: &quot;Sis Puella Magica&quot;, a heartbreaking ballad of longing and loss that sets the tone for &quot;Puella Madoka Magi Magica&quot;<br /> <br /> More to come later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=btmSuNcxiIU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=btmSuNcxiIU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=btmSuNcxiIU </a> </div> <div class=\